msgstr ""

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
msgctxt "help.letters.line"
msgid "What readers send a piece and its writer."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "help.letters.p1"
msgid "<b>Under every piece, readers write letters and can thank the writer with a tip.</b>"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "help.letters.p2"
msgid "To write a letter: type it in the box under the piece and post it. Letters are public, with your name and country. You can withdraw your own letter from its ⋯."
msgstr ""

#. {paperShare} is a percentage, printed without the percent sign. {minimumTip} is the smallest tip, drawn as a coin amount.
msgctxt "help.letters.p3"
msgid "To thank the writer: press Thank and choose an amount, from {minimumTip}. The writer keeps most of it and the paper keeps the rest ({paperShare}% unless its owner changes it). You thank a writer once for each piece."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "help.letters.p4"
msgid "To say what you thought: Good piece or Not for me. To report a letter or a piece, open its ⋯."
msgstr ""

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
msgctxt "help.letters.title"
msgid "How do letters and tips work?"
msgstr ""

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
msgctxt "help.market.line"
msgid "Buying, selling, and what a trade costs."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "help.market.p1"
msgid "<b>Every good has a page in the Market, with its price delivered to where you are and one button that buys or sells.</b>"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "help.market.p2"
msgid "To buy: open the good, choose Buy and how many, and press the button. It shows the total, and that is what you pay. The cheapest offers are taken first."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "help.market.p3"
msgid "To sell: choose Sell. Sell now sells to the buyers paying most; when nobody is buying, set your own price."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "help.market.p4"
msgid "To set your own price: press Set your own price. An offer to buy sets its money aside and a listing holds your goods, until one is taken."
msgstr ""

#. {percent} is a percentage, printed without the percent sign. {amount} is the size of a trade that asks first, drawn as a coin amount.
msgctxt "help.market.p5"
msgid "The total is the price, freight by weight and distance, a fee of {percent}% paid to the country the goods are delivered to, and an import tax on goods from another country. A trade of {amount} or more asks you first."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "help.market.p6"
msgid "Until a country’s players make enough, the game’s shop sells food, construction materials, industrial components and fuel in its capital, at a price anyone who makes it can sell for less."
msgstr ""

msgctxt "help.market.p7"
msgid "Words: Delivered: the price with every charge, to where you are. Bid: an offer to buy at your own price."
msgstr ""

#. The question this page answers; also its door on Help's front page. Screens and buttons named in Help's text must match the interface's own wording.
msgctxt "help.market.title"
msgid "How do I buy and sell?"
msgstr ""

msgctxt "help.moderation.answer"
msgid "Read the report, decide it within 24 hours, and check the words the player will read before you send them."
msgstr ""

#. One short line under the title on the page's door; keep it short.
msgctxt "help.moderation.line"
msgid "For staff: the queue, a decision, and an appeal."
msgstr ""

#. Follows the step's bold start and its colon, so it begins in lower case in English.
msgctxt "help.moderation.step1.how"
msgid "open the staff console: reports are oldest first, and one waiting more than 24 hours says Late."
msgstr ""

#. The bold start of one step, before a colon: what the player wants to do.
msgctxt "help.moderation.step1.to"
msgid "To see what waits"
msgstr ""

#. Follows the step's bold start and its colon, so it begins in lower case in English.
msgctxt "help.moderation.step2.how"
msgid "open a report, press Decide, and choose what it stops and for how long."
msgstr ""

#. The bold start of one step, before a colon: what the player wants to do.
msgctxt "help.moderation.step2.to"
msgid "To decide"
msgstr ""

#. Follows the step's bold start and its colon, so it begins in lower case in English.
msgctxt "help.moderation.step3.how"
msgid "the question shows the player's sentence, who is told, and that they may appeal."
msgstr ""

#. The bold start of one step, before a colon: what the player wants to do.
msgctxt "help.moderation.step3.to"
msgid "To check the words"
msgstr ""

#. Follows the step's bold start and its colon, so it begins in lower case in English.
msgctxt "help.moderation.step4.how"
msgid "press Nothing was wrong. Close it."
msgstr ""

#. The bold start of one step, before a colon: what the player wants to do.
msgctxt "help.moderation.step4.to"
msgid "To close one with nothing wrong"
msgstr ""

#. Follows the step's bold start and its colon, so it begins in lower case in English.
msgctxt "help.moderation.step5.how"
msgid "a moderator who did not decide it reads it, and presses Lift it or Keep it."
msgstr ""

#. The bold start of one step, before a colon: what the player wants to do.
msgctxt "help.moderation.step5.to"
msgid "To answer an appeal"
msgstr ""

#. Everyday words a player might type into Help's search to find this page, separated by commas. Give the words people in your language would search with, and add others if you like. Keep the commas.
